Z||000000||elfiero||05-22-2001||03:59 PM||||Ok,Here's the deal,my new stock clutch is<BR>slipping when I get on it(TPIV8,isuzu5sp)<BR>ya-ya I know,should have put in a good one<BR>the first time!so I'm looking for the best<BR>I can find-I read all the stuff in the <BR>archives,anything new?I don't like to use<BR>this expression,but money is not an issue.<BR>however,streetability is-no sintered bronze,<BR>solid hub, chatterboxes for me. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||88formula||05-22-2001||05:22 PM||||I like the kevlar clutch that the Fieroshop sells. To help you get more of your power to the rear wheels I recommend you get his aluminum flywheel too. <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bruce||05-22-2001||05:35 PM||||I've heard good things about the Centerforce dual-friction clutch.<BR>If you've been following the forum, there seems to be some kind of conflict among forum members and the Fiero Shop owners. I'm not to sure what the deal is, though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||05-22-2001||05:52 PM||||I would go with the Centerforce with a V8, mainly because Archie recommends it and he probably has the most experience with SBC Fieros on the Forum.  There are no doubt better out there, but I think the Centerforce probably has the balance of strength and streetability you're looking for.  That's what I'm going with next time I do a clutch (unless something changes my mind between now and then).||||reg||4
Z||000004||Phil||05-22-2001||07:06 PM||||I'm sure Archie will correct me if I am in error but the Center Force that Archie sells in not the same one you get if you order it directly from CF. Archie has them made up to different specs.||||reg||1
